WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
Can you tell what something is without looking?

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:08.620
A pillowcase and a few everyday objects let your child find out what skin can sense.

3
00:00:11.683 --> 00:00:15.303
The bag takes sight away, so touch has to do the job alone.

4
00:00:16.643 --> 00:00:21.463
Your child practices describing what they feel, making a guess, and checking it with

5
00:00:21.463 --> 00:00:24.863
their eyes. It takes about twenty-five minutes.

6
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:29.783
You need a pillowcase and eight to ten objects with different textures.

7
00:00:31.243 --> 00:00:35.623
Think of a pinecone, a large smooth stone, a new sponge, a wool mitten, and an

8
00:00:35.623 --> 00:00:41.303
orange. Keep a metal spoon, a wooden spoon, and a spoon from the fridge aside.

9
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:43.957
Stay with your child throughout.

10
00:00:45.457 --> 00:00:46.957
Pack and check the objects yourself.

11
00:00:48.337 --> 00:00:51.897
Even when squeezed, they should be too big for a toilet paper tube.

12
00:00:53.217 --> 00:00:57.537
Skip anything sharp, hot, frozen, breakable, alive, or with loose parts.

13
00:00:58.857 --> 00:01:00.597
Keep all bag objects out of mouths.

14
00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:05.690
Your child puts one hand in and holds one object without looking.

15
00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:08.590
Say, 'Don't tell me what it is yet.

16
00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:11.010
Tell me what it feels like.'

17
00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:14.930
Ask for three describing words, like bumpy, hard, and light.

18
00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:17.290
Write them down.

19
00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.833
Have your child guess, then pull out the object.

20
00:01:22.413 --> 00:01:24.113
Compare what they felt with what they can see.

21
00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:27.193
Their hand could feel the shape and bumps.

22
00:01:28.493 --> 00:01:29.893
Their eyes can see the color.

23
00:01:30.917 --> 00:01:34.437
Next, put the metal spoon and the wooden spoon in the bag.

24
00:01:35.597 --> 00:01:37.357
They have been in the same room all day.

25
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.520
Both spoons are at room temperature.

26
00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:42.820
What do you predict?

27
00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.900
When your child feels both spoons, will one feel colder?

28
00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:57.483
The metal spoon usually feels colder because it draws heat from fingers faster.

29
00:01:59.023 --> 00:02:00.023
Dry the fridge spoon.

30
00:02:01.183 --> 00:02:03.223
Hand it over with your child’s eyes closed.

31
00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:05.843
Ask whether it feels wet.

32
00:02:07.143 --> 00:02:09.743
Wipe the spoon with a dry towel and check the towel.

33
00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:15.483
If your child felt wetness and the towel stays dry, the cold may explain the

34
00:02:15.483 --> 00:02:19.143
feeling. A damp spot can come from condensation.

35
00:02:20.283 --> 00:02:22.303
Ask your child to close their eyes.

36
00:02:23.703 --> 00:02:28.203
Brush a craft feather over a fingertip, the back of the hand, an elbow, and a foot.

37
00:02:29.603 --> 00:02:30.823
Ask where they felt it best.

38
00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:35.903
Then label five cards for eyes, ears, nose, tongue, and skin.

39
00:02:37.343 --> 00:02:38.843
Sort the describing words together.

40
00:02:39.917 --> 00:02:41.837
Stay with your child the whole time.

41
00:02:43.117 --> 00:02:48.137
Keep small things like marbles, beads, coins, batteries, and magnets away from

42
00:02:48.137 --> 00:02:49.157
children under four.

43
00:02:50.457 --> 00:02:52.437
Call nine one one if a child is choking.

44
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:58.920
Check for allergies first, and leave out balloons and rubber gloves if anyone has a

45
00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.220
latex allergy. Use a craft-store feather.

46
00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.180
Everyone washes hands afterward.

47
00:03:06.283 --> 00:03:09.763
End by asking, 'What could your hand tell you about the orange?

48
00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:12.623
What could only your eyes tell you?'

49
00:03:13.283 --> 00:03:15.203
Skin found shape, texture, and cold.

50
00:03:16.643 --> 00:03:17.423
Eyes found color.
